---
title: Hardware Info
order: 1
description: Device enumeration and system hardware details
tags: [hardware, lspci, lsusb, lscpu, dmidecode, hwinfo]
---

Querying hardware information on Artix/Arch Linux systems.

@code bash
# CPU information
lscpu                            # architecture, cores, threads, cache
lscpu -e                         # extended per-CPU table
lscpu -J                         # JSON output
cat /proc/cpuinfo                # raw kernel CPU info

# PCI devices (GPUs, NICs, controllers)
lspci                            # list all PCI devices
lspci -v                         # verbose (capabilities, drivers)
lspci -vv                        # very verbose
lspci -k                         # show kernel drivers in use
lspci -nn                        # show vendor/device IDs
lspci -s 01:00.0 -v             # specific device by slot
lspci -d 10de: -v               # filter by vendor ID (NVIDIA=10de)
lspci | grep -i vga              # find graphics card
lspci | grep -i net              # find network adapters

# USB devices
lsusb                            # list all USB devices
lsusb -v                         # verbose
lsusb -t                         # tree view (hubs and ports)
lsusb -s 001:003                 # specific bus:device
lsusb -d 046d:c52b              # filter by vendor:product ID

@text
dmidecode reads hardware info from SMBIOS/DMI tables (requires root).
hwinfo provides a comprehensive hardware probe.

@code bash
# DMI/SMBIOS tables (requires root)
sudo dmidecode                   # full dump
sudo dmidecode -t bios           # BIOS info
sudo dmidecode -t system         # system manufacturer/model/serial
sudo dmidecode -t baseboard      # motherboard info
sudo dmidecode -t memory         # RAM slots, size, speed, type
sudo dmidecode -t processor      # CPU socket details
sudo dmidecode -t chassis        # case type
sudo dmidecode -s system-product-name   # single string value

# hwinfo (install: pacman -S hwinfo)
sudo hwinfo --short              # summary of all hardware
sudo hwinfo --cpu
sudo hwinfo --disk
sudo hwinfo --network
sudo hwinfo --gfxcard
sudo hwinfo --sound
sudo hwinfo --usb
sudo hwinfo --pci

@text
Additional hardware info sources from /proc and /sys.

@code bash
# Block devices
lsblk                           # block device tree
lsblk -f                        # filesystems and UUIDs
lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,TYPE,MOUNTPOINT,MODEL

# Memory
free -h                          # RAM summary
cat /proc/meminfo                # detailed memory stats

# Kernel modules (drivers)
lsmod                           # loaded kernel modules
modinfo <module>                 # module details
lspci -k                        # PCI devices with their modules

# All hardware overview
inxi -Fxz                       # comprehensive summary (install: pacman -S inxi)
